Accept the model path /v1/models itself advertises.

/v1/models publishes each entry's root (the checkpoint path), but the name
check matched the served name only, so a client that echoed the root back --
the obvious "use what the server told me" move -- got a 404. is_base_model
now accepts the served name, the full model path, or the path's basename,
all as exact matches: nothing fuzzy, nothing prefix-matched. This removes
the failure class for every client, including ones the operator does not
control.

